          "marker": "20",
          "normalized_marker": "20",
          "occurrence": 1,
          "source_text": "96. The 1732 rule that tried to force families to declare their mad members imposed a penalty of 80 strokes of the heavy stick if failure to comply led a mad person to commit suicide (see Appendix 8). In Chapter 8 I showed that physicians and common people alike often attributed suicides to ghosts.",
          "page_no": 523,
          "display_marker": "20",
          "source_marker": "20",
          "title_hint": "",
          "created_at": 1777755996,
